SCP-firmware v2.11.0's scmi_perf module (with its fast channels and
plugins handler) and CIX's changes to it:
- protocol version 3.0; fast-channel rate limit at least 1 ms;
- configuration: perf_doms_enabled, the domains SCMI drives (a level set
  on another is answered SUCCESS and ignored), and tdp_opp_run, per DxS
  domain the frequency the DPM allows under the TDP;
- perf_set_level: a level locked by locked_perf is set as it is; otherwise
  it is capped to the highest OPP within the TDP frequency
  (find_opp_for_freq) and checked against the locked limits if any; the
  level set is written to the domain's level-get fast channel;
- the fast-channel pass (fast_channels_process): domains from the third on
  among those SCMI drives, with or without fast channels; a plugin that
  does not answer FWK_SUCCESS ends it (sky1soc_perf answers FWK_PENDING
  and applies the CPU levels itself); levels set go to the level-get fast
  channels; one pass is scheduled at a time unless forced
  (fast_channel_callback), sky1soc_perf can schedule one;
- on_fast_channel_interrupt (CIX's mailbox handler calls it when the AP
  writes a fast channel): the GPU's level is applied at once, both GPU
  clocks from CIX's frequency pairs (search_for_freq), then a pass;
- on_tdp_notify and the TDP_NOTIFICATION event: domains whose TDP
  frequency changed are set again;
- sky1soc_perf may bind the DVFS update API; a missing sustained OPP
  (dvfs: FWK_E_RANGE) leaves level 0 in the fast channels;
- the plugins handler: equal limits are valid, the full-view sync takes
  the plugin's level, and update returns the first plugin status that is
  not FWK_SUCCESS (and stops there).
Upstream's fast-channel pass for builds without the plugins handler is
left out (CIX's build has the handler).
Everything else is upstream's (BSD-3-Clause, see
../../../SCP-firmware/license.md).
